"seg":7,"note":"Seat of the Roman governor, Sergius Paulus, who believed. From here on, Luke calls Saul by the name Paul."},{"p":"per","ref":"Acts 13:13","seg":4,"sea":1,"note":"John Mark left them here and went back to Jerusalem."},{"p":"antP","ref":"Acts 13:14-52","seg":9,"note":"Paul's first recorded sermon. Many Gentiles believed. Opposition drove them out of the region."},{"p":"ico","ref":"Acts 14:1-6","seg":6,"note":"A great number of Jews and Greeks believed. When a plot to stone them formed, they fled."},{"p":"lys","ref":"Acts 14:8-20","seg":11,"note":"Paul healed a man lame from birth. The crowd called them gods. Later Paul was stoned and left for dead."},{"p":"der","ref":"Acts 14:20-21","seg":2,"note":"They made many disciples. Then they turned back the way they came."},{"p":"lys","ref":"Acts 14:21-22","seg":3,"ret":1,"note":"They strengthened the disciples and urged them to remain true to the faith."},{"p":"ico","ref":"Acts 14:21-22","seg":0,"ret":1,"note":"They encouraged the believers to keep the faith through hardship."},{"p":"antP","ref":"Acts 14:21-23","seg":1,"ret":1,"note":"They appointed elders in each church, with prayer and fasting."},{"p":"per","ref":"Acts 14:24-25","seg":10,"ret":1,"note":"This time they preached the word in Perga."},{"p":"att","ref":"Acts 14:25-26","seg":8,"ret":1,"note":"The port where they boarded a ship for Syria."},{"p":"antS","ref":"Acts 14:26-28","seg":12,"sea":1,"ret":1,"trim":1,"note":"They gathered the church and reported how God had opened a door of faith to the Gentiles."}],"labels":{"antS":["Antioch","in Syria","above"],"sel":["Seleucia","","endb"],"sal":["Salamis","","start"],"pap":["Paphos","","below"],"per":["Perga","","above"],"att":["Attalia","","endb"],"antP":["Antioch","in Pisidia","above"],"ico":["Iconium","","start"],"lys":["Lystra","","end"],"der":["Derbe","","start"]},"regions":[[33.15,35.1,"CYPRUS"],[31.75,37.02,"PAMPHYLIA"],[32.3,38.85,"GALATIA"],[33.05,38.2,"LYCAONIA"],[35.75,37.35,"CILICIA"],[36.75,